    <!-- =====================================
         OVERVIEW
    ====================================== -->

    <section class="section" id="overview">

      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <div class="section-number">01 / Concept</div>
          <div class="section-title">The Nereus system</div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-description">
          An infrastructure strategy centered around reuse, vertical
          density and offshore resources.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="overview card">

        <div class="overview-grid">

          <div class="overview-copy">

            <h2>
              Reuse what already exists.
            </h2>

            <p>
              Offshore oil rigs were engineered around substantial
              structural loads, including drilling equipment, cranes,
              machinery and operating infrastructure.
            </p>

            <p>
              Nereus uses that existing platform as the foundation for a
              vertically organized data center instead of constructing an
              entirely new offshore support structure.
            </p>

            <p>
              The proposed architecture concentrates the facility around a
              central vertical service spine. Power, cooling and other
              infrastructure can therefore be organized vertically while
              the computing areas are stacked through the structure.
            </p>

          </div>

          <div class="diagram">

            <div class="diagram-grid"></div>

            <div class="diagram-label label-power">
              WIND POWER
            </div>

            <div class="diagram-label label-data">
              DATA CENTER
            </div>

            <div class="diagram-label label-cooling">
              DEEP-SEA COOLING
            </div>

            <div class="rig">

              <div class="rig-top"></div>

              <div class="rig-body"></div>

              <div class="rig-platform platform-1"></div>
              <div class="rig-platform platform-2"></div>
              <div class="rig-platform platform-3"></div>
              <div class="rig-platform platform-4"></div>

            </div>

            <div class="water">
              <div class="water-label">
                Ocean / Cooling Source
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================
         ARCHITECTURE
    ====================================== -->

    <section class="section" id="architecture">

      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <div class="section-number">02 / Architecture</div>
          <div class="section-title">Stacking the rig</div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-description">
          Vertical organization is central to the Nereus concept.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principles">

        <article class="principle card">
          <div class="principle-number">01</div>

          <h3>Existing structural capacity</h3>

          <p>
            Offshore platforms are designed around significant structural
            and equipment loads. Nereus proposes using the existing
            structural system as the starting point for redevelopment.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle card">
          <div class="principle-number">02</div>

          <h3>Vertical density</h3>

          <p>
            Stacking the facility vertically allows more usable computing
            area to occupy the existing footprint while limiting the need
            for additional offshore extensions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle card">
          <div class="principle-number">03</div>

          <h3>Central infrastructure spine</h3>

          <p>
            Cooling, power distribution and other utility infrastructure
            can be concentrated through the center of the structure,
            simplifying routing between levels.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================
         TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE
    ====================================== -->

    <section class="section">

      <div class="technical-grid">

        <article class="technical-card card full">

          <div class="technical-icon">01</div>

          <h3>Natural vertical heat movement</h3>

          <p>
            A vertically stacked building provides an opportunity to
            organize thermal exhaust around the natural tendency of warm
            air to rise. The proposed design would place exhaust paths
            toward upper sections of the structure.
          </p>

          <p>
            The exact effectiveness of passive convection would depend on
            the final building envelope, equipment density, airflow design,
            external conditions and required data-center operating
            temperatures.
          </p>

        </article>

        <article class="technical-card card">

          <div class="technical-icon">02</div>

          <h3>Reduced routing complexity</h3>

          <p>
            Locating computing areas vertically around shared infrastructure
            could reduce the distance between systems and consolidate
            mechanical and electrical distribution.
          </p>

        </article>

        <article class="technical-card card">

          <div class="technical-icon">03</div>

          <h3>Emergency energy reserve</h3>

          <p>
            Under the concept's stated energy estimate, approximately nine
            percent of generated electricity would remain available as a
            potential surplus for battery storage or other emergency
            applications.
          </p>

        </article>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================
         SYSTEM FLOW
    ====================================== -->

