      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <div class="section-number">03 / System flow</div>
          <div class="section-title">How Nereus functions</div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-description">
          Five connected infrastructure systems form the proposed operating
          model.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flow card">

        <div class="flow-list">

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-number">01</div>
            <h4>Wind generation</h4>
            <p>
              Offshore turbines generate electricity for the facility.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-number">02</div>
            <h4>Power distribution</h4>
            <p>
              Electricity is routed into the data center and supporting
              infrastructure.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-number">03</div>
            <h4>Seawater cooling</h4>
            <p>
              Cold seawater is pumped through the cooling infrastructure.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-number">04</div>
            <h4>Aeolus filtration</h4>
            <p>
              Water and exhaust streams enter the proposed algae system.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-number">05</div>
            <h4>Ocean return</h4>
            <p>
              Treated water is returned toward the marine environment.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================
         COOLING
    ====================================== -->

    <section class="section" id="cooling">

      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <div class="section-number">04 / Cooling</div>
          <div class="section-title">The ocean becomes the heat sink</div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-description">
          Nereus proposes using deep seawater as a cooling resource rather
          than relying on freshwater from land-based systems.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="technical-grid">

        <article class="technical-card card">

          <div class="technical-icon">SW</div>

          <h3>Seawater cooling</h3>

          <p>
            Cold seawater would be pumped upward through the rig and passed
            through a dedicated cooling system before being returned toward
            the ocean.
          </p>

          <p>
            The concept's stated objective is to reduce cooling-related
            electricity consumption while eliminating dependence on local
            freshwater grids for the primary cooling resource.
          </p>

        </article>

        <article class="technical-card card">

          <div class="technical-icon">40</div>

          <h3>Potential efficiency gain</h3>

          <p>
            The concept estimates that seawater cooling could reduce power
            use by up to 40 percent. This figure is a project estimate and
            would require detailed engineering validation for a specific
            site, climate and cooling architecture.
          </p>

        </article>

      </div>

    </section>


