      <div class="card accordion">

        <div class="accordion-item">

          <button class="accordion-button">
            Structural verification
            <span class="accordion-symbol">+</span>
          </button>

          <div class="accordion-content">
            <div class="accordion-content-inner">
              The existing platform would need a detailed structural
              assessment covering dead loads, live loads, equipment loads,
              wind, waves, fatigue, corrosion and the proposed additional
              data-center structure.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">

          <button class="accordion-button">
            Seawater environmental impact
            <span class="accordion-symbol">+</span>
          </button>

          <div class="accordion-content">
            <div class="accordion-content-inner">
              Intake and discharge systems would require detailed analysis
              of temperature differences, flow rates, marine organisms,
              chemical treatment and the effects of returning water to the
              surrounding environment.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">

          <button class="accordion-button">
            Turbine generation assumptions
            <span class="accordion-symbol">+</span>
          </button>

          <div class="accordion-content">
            <div class="accordion-content-inner">
              Actual generation would depend on turbine model, hub height,
              wind resource, wake effects, availability, maintenance,
              transmission losses and site-specific offshore conditions.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">

          <button class="accordion-button">
            Data-center power requirements
            <span class="accordion-symbol">+</span>
          </button>

          <div class="accordion-content">
            <div class="accordion-content-inner">
              The relationship between 142 million kWh of annual generation
              and actual facility demand would need to be modeled using
              rack density, PUE, utilization, redundancy, cooling load and
              seasonal operating conditions.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">

          <button class="accordion-button">
            Aeolus biological performance
            <span class="accordion-symbol">+</span>
          </button>

          <div class="accordion-content">
            <div class="accordion-content-inner">
              The proposed algae system would require laboratory and pilot
              testing to establish growth rates, CO₂ uptake, contaminant
              removal, temperature requirements, harvesting energy,
              byproduct economics and environmental performance.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================
         FOOTER
    ====================================== -->

    <footer>

      <div class="footer-top">

        <div>

          <div class="footer-brand">
            Nereus
          </div>

          <div class="footer-copy">
            Offshore data infrastructure built around the adaptive reuse of
            existing marine structures, renewable generation, seawater
            cooling and integrated biological filtration.
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="footer-note">
          CONCEPT DEVELOPMENT<br>
          NEREUS / AEOLOUS
        </div>

      </div>

    </footer>

  </main>


  <!-- =====================================
       PROJECT BRIEF MODAL
  ====================================== -->

  <div class="modal-overlay" id="modal">

    <div class="modal">

      <div class="modal-header">

        <div class="modal-title">
          Nereus project brief
        </div>

        <button class="modal-close" id="modalClose">
          ×
        </button>

      </div>

      <p>
        Nereus is a proposed offshore infrastructure concept that combines
        a vertically stacked data center with an existing modified offshore
        oil-rig structure. The concept incorporates offshore wind power,
        seawater cooling, battery storage and the proposed Aeolus
        microalgae filtration system.
      </p>

      <br>

      <p>
        The figures presented throughout this website are the current
        conceptual assumptions supplied for the Nereus proposal. They are
        not represented as completed engineering calculations or
        independently verified performance results.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <script>

    /* =========================================
       SCROLL PROGRESS
    ========================================= */

    const progress = document.getElementById("scrollProgress");

    window.addEventListener("scroll", () => {

      const scrollTop = window.scrollY;
      const documentHeight =
        document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;

      const percentage =
        documentHeight > 0
          ? (scrollTop / documentHeight) * 100
          : 0;

      progress.style.width = percentage + "%";

    });


    /* =========================================
       NAV ACTIVE STATES
    ========================================= */

    const sections = document.querySelectorAll(
      "section[id]"
    );

    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll(
      ".nav-link"
    );

    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      entries => {

        entries.forEach(entry => {

          if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;

          navLinks.forEach(link => {
            link.classList.remove("active");
          });

          const active = document.querySelector(
            `.nav-link[href="#${entry.target.id}"]`
          );

          if (active) {
            active.classList.add("active");
          }

        });

      },
      {
        rootMargin: "-25% 0px -65% 0px"
      }
    );

    sections.forEach(section => {
      observer.observe(section);
    });


    /* =========================================
       ACCORDIONS
    ========================================= */

    document.querySelectorAll(
      ".accordion-item"
    ).forEach(item => {

      const button =
        item.querySelector(".accordion-button");

      const content =
        item.querySelector(".accordion-content");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {

        const isOpen =
          item.classList.contains("open");

        item.classList.toggle("open");

        if (isOpen) {

          content.style.maxHeight = "0px";

        } else {

          content.style.maxHeight =
            content.scrollHeight + "px";

        }

      });

      if (item.classList.contains("open")) {
        content.style.maxHeight =
          content.scrollHeight + "px";
      }

    });


    /* =========================================
       MODAL
    ========================================= */

    const modal =
      document.getElementById("modal");

    const infoButton =
      document.getElementById("infoButton");

    const modalClose =
      document.getElementById("modalClose");

    infoButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
      modal.classList.add("active");
      document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
    });

    modalClose.addEventListener("click", closeModal);

    modal.addEventListener("click", event => {

      if (event.target === modal) {
        closeModal();
      }

    });

    function closeModal() {
      modal.classList.remove("active");
      document.body.style.overflow = "";
    }


    /* =========================================
       ESCAPE KEY
    ========================================= */

    document.addEventListener("keydown", event => {

      if (event.key === "Escape") {
        closeModal();
      }

    });


    /* =========================================
       BUTTON MICRO-INTERACTIONS
    ========================================= */

    document.querySelectorAll(
      ".primary-button, .secondary-button"
    ).forEach(button => {

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {

        button.style.transform =
          "translateY(1px)";

        setTimeout(() => {
          button.style.transform = "";
        }, 120);

      });

    });

  </script>

</body>
</html>
